Generate 1 sabotage suggestion for an single_responsibility task in javascript.

Language syntax reference:
JavaScript OOP:
- Class: class Animal { constructor(name) { this.name = name; } speak() { return this.name; } }
- Inheritance: class Dog extends Animal { constructor(name) { super(name); } }
- Private: use #field syntax or closures. Use #balance for private fields.
- Polymorphism: override methods in subclass, no keyword needed

Task prompt: Our GameItem class is doing too much! It's currently responsible for both the item's core game logic and its visual representation. Refactor the code by creating a separate ItemDisplay class to handle all presentation concerns, adhering to the Single Responsibility Principle.

Current code in the editor:
```
class GameItem {
    constructor(id, name, type, iconUrl) {
        this.id = id;
        this.name = name;
        this.type = type;
        this.iconUrl = iconUrl; // This property belongs to display
    }

    getInfo() {
        return `${this.name} (${this.type})`;
    }

    // TODO: This method has a display responsibility. Move it to a new class!
    renderIcon() {
        return `<img src="${this.iconUrl}" alt="${this.name}">`;
    }

    // TODO: This method has a display responsibility. Move it to a new class!
    getDisplayDescription() {
        return `A rare ${this.type} named ${this.name}.`;
    }
}

// Example usage (will need adjustment after refactoring)
const sword = new GameItem('s123', 'Excalibur', 'Legendary Sword', '/icons/sword.png');
console.log(sword.getInfo());
console.log(sword.renderIcon());
console.log(sword.getDisplayDescription());
```

